From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] compat: match the PS4 SDK's ptrace signature.

The PS5 SDK declares ptrace's address argument as caddr_t, FreeBSD's
spelling. The OpenOrbis PS4 SDK (sys/ptrace.h:109) declares it void *:

    int ptrace(int _request, pid_t _pid, void* _addr, int _data);

caddr_t is char *, so the two differ only in the pointer's type and not
in the ABI, but C still rejects the definition as a conflicting type.
Use void * so the definition matches on PS4; the body ignores every
argument and returns the failure stub either way.
---
 wine/ps5/pw_wine_compat_libc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
diff --git a/wine/ps5/pw_wine_compat_libc.c b/wine/ps5/pw_wine_compat_libc.c
index 0de4656..8ffd6aa 100644
--- a/wine/ps5/pw_wine_compat_libc.c
+++ b/wine/ps5/pw_wine_compat_libc.c
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ int posix_fadvise(int fd,off_t offset,off_t length,int advice)
 unsigned int if_nametoindex(const char *name){return pw_compat_if_nametoindex(name);}
 int fstatfs(int fd,struct statfs *buf){(void)fd;(void)buf;return pw_compat_no_fstatfs();}
 int link(const char *from,const char *to){(void)from;(void)to;return pw_compat_no_link();}
-int ptrace(int request,pid_t pid,caddr_t address,int data)
+int ptrace(int request,pid_t pid,void *address,int data)
 {(void)request;(void)pid;(void)address;(void)data;return (int)pw_compat_no_ptrace();}
 mode_t umask(mode_t mask){return pw_compat_umask(mask);}
 char *nl_langinfo(nl_item item){return (char *)(item==CODESET?pw_compat_codeset():"");}
